 "notes": "Constraint from neutron star observations (thermal relaxation, cooling, pulsar glitches) on exceptionally light QCD axions. Reported for Scenario A (K_\u03c3=0, no modification to nuclear interactions) as the most conservative bound. Extracted from Figure 18 lower boundary (most stringent constraint). The constraint excludes parameter space in the (m_a, 1/f_a) plane based on the requirement that neutron star crusts maintain minimum thickness (thermal relaxation constraint is dominant). For m_a \u2273 2\u00d710^-9 eV, \u03b5 < 0.2 is excluded, corresponding to a bound on 1/f_a derived from the axion mass formula m_a = 5.7 \u03bceV \u00d7 (10^12 GeV / f_a).",
